<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies eight issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies eight issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp said it has qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Jefferson UHSD, Calif., $6 million general obligation bonds, elective.</p>
<p>--Waterloo, Iowa, $4 million sewer revenue bonds and $4.5 million GOs as a direct purchase.</p>
<p>--Lewiston, Maine, $3.070 million public improvement GOs.</p>
<p>--Spartanburg County SD#5, S.C., $4.1 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Austin, Texas, $18.4 million tax bonds, elective.</p>
<p>--North Texas Muni Water, Texas, $7.125 million revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--San Antonio, Texas, $2.73 million special assessment bonds as a direct purchase.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
</text>
